      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فيّد مِنْ قِرْنِهِ</span></b>  (Th, M, L) <i>He turned away
from,</i> or <i>avoided, his adversary:</i> (Th, L:) or <i>he
fled from him.</i> (M.) [See a similar meaning of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فاد</span>, above.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فيّد</span>, (T, O, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفْيِيدٌ</span>,
(L, K,) <i>He augured evil from the cry of the</i> [<i>bird
called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيَّاد</span>. (T, O, L, K.)

